course: dictionary
lesson: 8992
title: Sixth and sixths
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sixth can be a number in order, like first, second, third. «Mia's sofa fitted five, and the sixth kid always ended up on the floor.» Here sixth means the number 6 in the line, after the fifth kid.
explain: A sixth, with no number before it, is a fraction. It is one of six equal parts of a whole, written 1/6. Sixths means more than one of those parts, like 5/6.
explain: Look at the words around it to know which meaning is right. If the sentence is about a line or a list, it is an order word. If it is about sharing something into equal parts, it is a fraction.
fact: Sixth means number 6 in order, after the fifth.
fact: A sixth is one of six equal parts of a whole, written 1/6.
fact: To find a sixth of a number, divide it by 6: a sixth of 30 is 5.
fact: «The Moon's gravity is about one sixth of the Earth's gravity.» So you would feel much lighter on the Moon.
fact: A sixth sense is a feeling that you know something without seeing or hearing it.
exercise: «The sixth kid always ended up on the floor.» What does sixth mean here? | The first one | One of six equal parts | *Number six in order, after the fifth | A feeling that you know something
exercise: What is a sixth of 30? | 6 | 24 | 36 | *5
exercise: Which fraction is one sixth? | *1/6 | 1/5 | 1/60 | 6/1
test: «The Moon's gravity is about one sixth of the Earth's gravity.» What fraction of Earth's gravity is that? | 1/2 | 6/1 | *1/6 | 1/60
test: What is a sixth of 18? | 12 | 6 | 2 | *3
exam: Your sixth sense tells you that something is wrong, even though you cannot see or hear it. What is a sixth sense? | A loud noise that wakes you up | The sixth number in a list of senses | *A feeling that you know something without seeing or hearing it | A sixth of a sense, like one part of your eyes
